      "completion_tokens": 1132,
      "output": "At its most basic level, **water** is a chemical substance with the chemical formula **$H_2O$**. This means that each molecule of water is made up of two hydrogen atoms bonded to one oxygen atom.\n\nHere is a breakdown of what makes water unique and important:\n\n### 1. Molecular Structure\nWater is a **polar molecule**. Because oxygen is more \"thirsty\" for electrons than hydrogen, the oxygen end of the molecule has a slight negative charge, and the hydrogen ends have a slight positive charge. This polarity allows water molecules to stick to one another (cohesion) and to other substances (adhesion), which is why water forms droplets and flows.\n\n### 2. The Three States of Matter\nWater is one of the few substances on Earth that naturally exists as a solid, liquid, and gas at the temperatures typically found on our planet:\n*   **Solid (Ice):** When frozen, the molecules lock into a rigid crystal lattice.\n*   **Liquid:** The most common state, where molecules move freely but stay close together.\n*   **Gas (Steam/Vapor):** When heated, molecules move so fast they escape the liquid surface.\n\n### 3. The Universal Solvent\nWater is often called the \"universal solvent\" because it can dissolve more substances than any other liquid. This is critical for life because it allows nutrients to be transported through the bloodstream and plants to absorb minerals from the soil.\n\n### 4. High Specific Heat Capacity\nWater can absorb a lot of heat without getting hot. This property helps regulate the Earth's climate and keeps the human body at a stable temperature.\n\n### 5. Essential for Life\nWater is the foundation of life as we know it. It is the primary component of all living cells (about 60% of the human body) and is necessary for:\n*   Digestion\n*   Temperature regulation (sweating)\n*   Lubricating joints\n*   Removing waste\n\nIn short, water is a transparent, odorless, tasteless liquid that is the physical basis of the hydrosphere and the medium in which all known life exists."
